# The library's own stores of elements test nothing by themselves. Under `--aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges` each holds its position and the kind of its list; three things more that its text leans on are held here.
# The store of an int32 writes the low half of the word alone: the place must bear the mark of an int32 already: a hole inside the length does not. The boxed store takes storage for int32s too: what is no int32 may not go into it.
# Under `--aot-harden=proof-checks` the store of a double holds that it does not store the word of a hole, as the store that the walk makes does.
